{"id":"7c0dd540-ed8c-4af9-ada7-fddcbf325080","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"84647257dc716d2a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/sourcemap.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8dc55969ab659becd90b1e7abe9bf5c96a781bc7","start":1,"end":94},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","SourceMap","{","\"","sources","\"",":","string","[]",";","\"","sourceRoot","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","mappings","\"",":","string","}"]},"context":{"after":"4bc015cdb7c3df9d"}},"payload":{"text":"Source maps, read: where a position in generated code (what the dev server serves) came from in the source (what's in\nthe workspace). Enough of the format (v3) to answer that — `sources` and `mappings`, the base64 VLQ segments — for the\ninline maps the preview's dev server writes (`//# sourceMappingURL=data:…`), so a profile's hotspot lands on the line\nyou wrote rather than the line it compiled to.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:34.324Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:34.324Z"}
{"id":"7f5c6cd1-529a-4fa9-a75d-4af11933ef14","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"978089a2d8f7e626","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/sourcemap.ts","baseline":{"blob":"17dbbe82c37136917c01067bb3125ab628a167d7","start":2380,"end":2394},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["let","source","=","0"]},"context":{"before":"eb97996470d572f4#0","after":"82a28592eac6e6de"}},"payload":{"text":"Source, line and column are relative to the previous segment's across the whole map; the generated column, to the\nprevious segment's on the same line. So decode up to `line`, carrying them.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:29.307Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:02:29.307Z"}
